# An eighth Russian story: Masha's day
subtitle: "Read Masha's day in Moscow, fourteen lines built from lessons 1–79 with only eight glosses: getting dressed, cooking, an exam, a bad phone line, a jacket in a shop, dinner out and a cough. Hear it line by line, test yourself by eye and by ear, say a line, and look back at unit eight."
tags: ["russian","russian reading","russian story","everyday russian","russian a2"]
teaches: ["reading/reading-stories"]
thumb: "band \"An eighth story: Masha's day\" note \"lessons 71–79, 14 lines\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Describing people in Russian: похо́ж на па́пу","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/81-russian-looks.cast"}

## An eighth Russian story: Masha's day
level: basic
heading: false

